    "seo": {
      "title": "Iran’s Technical & Vocational Training Organization | Iran, Unfolded",
      "description": "Explore TVTO’s documented role in skills training, instructor development, certification, and UNHCR-supported refugee training."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "organizational-role",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "An organization focused on occupational skills",
        "content": "The Technical and Vocational Training Organization, or TVTO, occupies a different institutional space from a university. UNESCO-UNEVOC identifies it with skills training and vocational qualifications and places it within the Ministry of Cooperatives, Labour and Social Welfare. Its Instructor Training Center in Karaj, west of Tehran, prepares instructors for TVTO and affiliated institutions. The centre was established in 1974 with assistance from the International Labour Organization and the United Nations Development Programme. [s1]\n\nCertification is a distinct part of this role. UNHCR’s public information explains that participants who complete TVTO courses and pass their final examinations receive official TVTO certificates. This supports recognition of assessed skills; it does not establish automatic recognition by foreign authorities or a guarantee of employment. UNHCR also links to TVTO’s website, providing the basis for the website field on this page. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "instructor-modernization",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Instructor development and modernization",
        "content": "UNESCO-UNEVOC describes a 2023–2028 project to modernize the Instructor Training Center, implemented with UNESCO Tehran and funded by the Korea International Cooperation Agency. Its stated purposes include improved teaching facilities and methods, staff development, and more relevant vocational learning. These describe intended changes rather than independently measured effects. [s3]\n\nA separate account records that the project was formally introduced in Iran on 17 December 2024 at the Karaj centre. The event included a project-office opening, demonstrations by the centre and its partners, and discussion of skills gaps among graduates. The reported launch is evidence of implementation activity, while remaining distinct from completion of the full programme. [s5]",
        "source_ids": ["s3", "s5"]
      },
      {
        "id": "refugee-programme",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A measurable partnership with a limited scope",
        "content": "UNHCR’s August 2023 livelihoods update reports annual participation in TVTO classes supported through its refugee programme. The figures below concern that partnership, not all TVTO trainees or all vocational learners in Iran. They show lower reported participation in each year after the series peak in 2019. The document does not establish why participation changed, and these counts should not be interpreted as employment outcomes. [s4]\n\nThe same update presents a 2023 training target. That target is excluded from the historical series because a planned beneficiary count is not equivalent to reported participation. The short series is retained because it has a consistent presentation within one inspected source; it is not extended with differently scoped figures from later publications. [s4]",
        "source_ids": ["s4"]
